A||||6||Oreif||Need help from anyone on AOL.||||5||
Z||000000||Oreif||11-01-2001||08:48 AM||||Here's the problem, a relative has a computer. 166mhz with 32M of ram. She has been on AOL for about a year now. Recently AOL has uploaded some "update" files that deal with some "Print Services" Since this has happened she cannot print from the AOL browser. I loaded in the updated printer driver for her HP722C printer and that did not help. It will print from windows and if I switch the browser to I.E., it will print.<BR>In the AOL browser, when you hit "print" a "print services" window pops up (never came up before) and says to "click OK to print 1 copy" But at this point the screen freezes and the mouse arrow disappears.<BR>We also re-load AOL 6.0 but as soon as we went on-line it uploaded this print services update.<BR>Has anyone else had this problem?<BR>Anyone know the cure?<P>(Now I know why I never used AOL.)<P>TIA,<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000001||thomas_l||11-01-2001||10:02 AM||||That's sorta weird. New versions of AOL are based on IE. The only thing I see is a pretty obvious resource issue. 166Mhz with 32MB RAM is gonna be a stretch for any 6.0 browser plus Windows. Don't get me wrong - I'm not bashing the system. But years of (non-AOL) Internet help desk experience say that low system resources = unpredictable applications. i.e. sometimes they work OK sometimes they don't. I wouldn't run anything better than a 4.0 version on a system like that. <P>Before you call tech support you ought to at least invest in some RAM. I just bought two 32MB 72-pin EDO sticks (64MB total) for my old Mac 6100 for $50 from Crucial Memory. Going from 16MB to 72MB is like night & day difference. At the same time, I bought two sticks of 256MB PC133 for my 1 year old Presario for $50 (yes - 512MB Woohoo!!).<P>Last but not least, you might check the newsgroups (deja.com is my favorite) before calling tech support.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||11-01-2001||10:06 AM||||Sounds like a software problem, on your computers end.  I have AOL and a HP722 printer running newer drivers off of the HP sight (v10.3 maybe... I am at work and cannot check) and it will print off the AOL browser.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-01-2001||10:22 AM||||thomas_I, Yeah I was kind of thinking the memory/resources could be an issue. Maybe I'll pick up some ram for her P.C. and see if that corrects it. It is my Aunt's computer and she has had it for a while. Mainly she uses it for Email and surfing the net occasionally for her arts and crafts stuff. I really don't think it's worth it to buy a new P.C. since she is only on-line for less than 10 hours a month.<P>Fformula, What is your computer speed and memory? Yes the updated printer driver is V10.3. I downloaded it off of HP's site and tried it but it didn't help. (It does accept the newer color cartridge now)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||11-01-2001||10:46 AM||||I know it doesn't help, but AOL 6.0 was completely *riddled* with bugs. Three friends of mine had to completely recover their hard drives after attempting to run the first release of 6.0 on their machines.<P>I'm still using 5.0, and I'll keep doing so until I absolutely have to upgrade... it's been working great for me.<P>I don't know the first thing about fixing software and/or driver problems, but if possible, you might want to try wiping out 6.0 and loading up 5.0 to see if that solves the problems...||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||11-01-2001||10:53 AM||||I understand that AOL just released version 7.0 also... I haven't tried it yet.  I too would suggest memory being a possible issue.  Check <A HREF="http://www.pricewatch.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pricewatch.com</A>  for good memory deals (they have 512MB PC133 chips, $25 for Generic, $44 for Brand name, at I believe 1st Choice Memory... check the site).||||reg||1
Z||000006||avengador1||11-01-2001||04:38 PM||||You could also try <A HREF="http://www.tigerdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tigerdirect.com</A>  they seem to have some good prices on memory now.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
